---
description: UI/UX rules for the children's educational app
alwaysApply: true
---

# UI/UX PRIORITY

This project is a highly visual and interactive educational application for children.

The AI must constantly improve the visual experience while preserving all business logic.

# VISUAL GOALS

Every screen, activity, game, panel, modal, card, menu, dashboard, reward system, or interaction should feel:

- Colorful
- Friendly
- Stimulating
- Dynamic
- Emotionally positive
- Highly visual
- Child-oriented
- Interactive
- Playful
- Gamified

# UI STYLE

Prefer:

- Rounded corners
- Large buttons
- Soft shadows
- Bright but balanced colors
- Animated feedback
- Smooth transitions
- Visual hierarchy
- Cute illustrations
- Large readable typography
- Friendly spacing
- Playful layouts
- Visual rewards
- Fun empty states
- Interactive hover/tap states
- Floating elements
- Progress indicators
- XP bars
- Stars
- Coins
- Achievement systems
- Mascots
- Cartoon-like UI

# CHILDREN EXPERIENCE RULES

The interface should feel similar in emotional quality to:

- Duolingo Kids
- PBS Kids
- Toca Boca
- Khan Academy Kids
- Pou minigames
- Nintendo-like interfaces

The app should prioritize:
- dopamine feedback
- positive reinforcement
- curiosity
- reward sensation
- exploration
- visual stimulation

# IMAGES & VISUAL ASSETS

ALWAYS take advantage of:

- existing images
- illustrations
- icons
- stickers
- emojis
- gradients
- SVGs
- animations
- visual assets already available in the project

Never leave sections visually empty if assets can improve them.

# LIBRARIES

Prefer using modern UI/animation libraries when needed:

- Framer Motion
- Lottie
- GSAP
- TailwindCSS
- shadcn/ui
- Lucide Icons

Only use libraries already compatible with the project stack unless explicitly approved.

# UX RULES

Every interaction should:
- feel rewarding
- feel responsive
- provide visual feedback
- avoid boredom
- avoid visually flat layouts
- avoid corporate/minimal sterile design

Always improve:
- spacing
- visual rhythm
- hierarchy
- accessibility
- clarity
- readability

# EMOJIS

Use emojis strategically when appropriate in:
- rewards
- badges
- notifications
- achievements
- onboarding
- positive feedback

Avoid emoji spam.

# RESPONSIVE DESIGN

UI must work correctly on:
- desktop
- tablet
- mobile

# IMPORTANT

The goal is NOT minimalism.

The goal is:
- engagement
- stimulation
- delight
- emotional connection
- playful learning